Let \(v,\widetilde v\in\mathbb{R}_+^d\), \(m\in\mathbb{R}^d\), and \(\varepsilon>0\). Define \(u(v)=m\oslash(\sqrt v+\varepsilon)\). If \(\|\widetilde v-v\|_\infty\le\eta\) and \(v_i,\widetilde v_i\ge
u>0\) for every coordinate, then \[\|u(\widetilde v)-u(v)\|_\infty\le rac{\|m\|_\infty\eta}{2\sqrt{
u}(\sqrt{
u}+\varepsilon)^2}.\] Thus a compression scheme may be evaluated through its reconstruction error \(\eta\), which bounds the induced coordinatewise update error under a positive state floor.
